Code that is written and compile-verified but NOT the live bot.

  iter5-expansion-reserve.patch   rejected as a no-op; re-open trigger recorded in
                                  TRAINING_LOG.md (chips visibly re-entering the
                                  1200-1350 band after a future accept).
  iter8-candidate/                the remembered-tower refill (package `bob`), held
                                  here only while iteration 7 occupies the evaluator.
                                  Durability, not strategy: a session died mid-run
                                  once and an uncommitted candidate would have gone
                                  with it.

Nothing here is built by gradle; src/ is the only source root.
  iter8-on-iter3/                 the SAME refill change rebased onto the iteration 3
                                  baseline, i.e. without iteration 7's tower-mix hash.
                                  Both variants exist so that iteration 8 is a single
                                  isolated change whichever way iteration 7 lands --
                                  iter8-candidate/ was built on the iteration 7 tree and
                                  would silently bundle the two if 7 were rejected.
  iter9-srp/                      see its own README.
